List of maintainers for open-dfp-34x-2c
=======================================

This file uses the Linux kernel MAINTAINERS format so that, once the kernel
tree is imported under linux/ and components are added, per-subsystem entries
can be written in the same style. Field letters used here:

	M: Maintainer -- the responsible person, with an e-mail address.
	S: Status -- Supported, Maintained, Odd Fixes, Orphan or Obsolete.
	F: Files and directories; wildcards allowed, a trailing slash means a
	   whole subtree.

As each component lands (see the per-directory READMEs and docs/adr/), it
gains its own section below. Kernel code under linux/ additionally keeps its
own entries in linux/MAINTAINERS, upstream style.

